# Workflow orchestration

This rule binds the kit's commands, agents, skills, state files, and hooks into one local-first, IDE-portable lifecycle. Each phase command (`core/common/commands/v0-*.md`) and skill (`SKILL.md`) holds its own procedure; this rule holds what applies to all of them.

Read `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` in the target repo for build/test commands, the Layout directory profile, and brownfield baseline exceptions before Build or Maintain. Profiles (`service`, `ui`, `app`) are defined in `project-delivery-core.mdc`. Filled Profile or root rows win; when still placeholders, `.agents-v0/scripts/resolve-layout.sh` resolves the profile matching files on disk.

## Lifecycle

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  roadmap[Roadmap] -->|gate| arch[Architecture]
  arch -->|gate| plan[Plan program]
  plan -->|gate| intake
  intake[Intake] -->|gate| design[Design]
  design -->|gate| build[Build]
  build -->|gate| verify[Verify]
  verify -->|gate| localrel[Local Release / Release]
  maintain[Maintain] --> verify
```

Phases: **Intake → Design → Build → Verify → Local Release (`/v0-local-release`) or Remote Release (`/v0-release`)**, with **Maintain** feeding into Verify. A new program of more than one story starts with **Roadmap** (`/v0-roadmap`), then **Architecture** (`/v0-architecture`), then **Plan** (`/v0-plan`). A single story starts at Intake. P0-A starts at Build. `/v0-export` and `/v0-deck` are documentation utilities, not phases. Full map: `docs/agents-v0/agents-v0-kit.md`.

## State and Phase Resume (`state.json`)

Workflow state, approved phases, `baseCommit`, and on-disk artifact pointers live in JSON state files managed by `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh`:
- Feature story: `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.state.json`
- Maintenance / Triage: `docs/agents-v0/maintain/<id>/state.json`
- Brownfield Onboard: `docs/agents-v0/onboarding/state.json`
- Program (Roadmap / Architecture / Plan): `docs/agents-v0/program.state.json`

| Field | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| `lastApprovedPhase` | Most recent approved phase (`intake`, `design`, `build`, `verify`, `release`, etc.). |
| `approvedPhases` | Ordered array of approved phases for this work item. |
| `phaseDates` | Map of approved phase → `YYYY-MM-DD` approval date (`intake`, `design`, `build`, etc.). |
| `activePhase` | Phase currently in flight (`onboard`, `roadmap`, `architecture`, `plan`, `intake`, `design`, `build`, `verify`, `release`, `maintain`). |
| `activeStatus` | `in_progress`, `awaiting_approval`, or `blocked`. |
| `blockedReason` | One-line reason when `activeStatus` is `blocked`. |
| `verifyPassed` | `true` when `/v0-verify` passes with zero Critical findings. |
| `reopenCount` | Number of times Verify re-opened Build/Maintain (capped at 3 before mandatory escalation). |
| `helperBriefHashes` | SHA-256 digests of prior helper briefs to prevent duplicate helper loops. |
| `artifacts` | Map of created artifact paths (`primary`, `design`, `openapi`, `buildPlan`, `buildReport`, `verify`) for fast context loading. |

- **Starting / Resuming a Phase:** Run `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh --active-phase <phase> --status in_progress <artifact>` and read the paths in `artifacts` from `<feature>.state.json` to continue from existing files on disk without recreating them.
- **Stopping at a Gate:** Write `<feature>.phase-result.md`, run `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh --active-phase <phase> --status awaiting_approval <artifact>`, and stop your turn. Never self-approve or infer approval.
- **Recording Human Approval:** Only after the user explicitly approves in chat (or records an `Approved` row in `Delivery approvals`), run `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh --approve <phase> <artifact>`.

`/v0-status` is read-only: it inspects the state file(s) and names the next command to run. When multiple features have state files and none is named by the user, list them and ask; never guess the newest `*.state.json`.

## Parallel Features

Each feature has its own `requirements/<feature>.md`, `<feature>.state.json`, `design/<feature>/`, `build/<feature>/`, and `verify/<feature>/`.
- **Worktree per feature (preferred):** Isolate concurrent features via `sh .agents-v0/scripts/feature-worktree.sh <feature>` (requires user confirmation).
- **Shared checkout safety:** Stop before editing shared files (`project-profile.md`, `openapi/`, `architecture.md`, `network.md`, `milestones/plan.md`, build/dependency manifests) if `git status` shows uncommitted changes from another feature.

## Change Tiers

| Tier | When | Path |
|------|------|------|
| **Trivial** | Docs-only or 1-for-1 patch version bump confirmed by the user | `/v0-triage` → `/v0-maintain` → abbreviated Verify (`/v0-verify`) |
| **Standard** | Feature or bugfix touching application code | Full Intake → Design (gate when contracts, UI, or Material apply) → Build → Verify → Local Release / Release |
| **Major** | New service, auth model, or cross-cutting architecture | Standard + ADR + threat-model notes in Design (`Material: yes` updates `arc-record.md`) |
| **Emergency** | User-confirmed production incident with rollback plan and `Follow-up verify due` date | `/v0-maintain` → immediate release; full `/v0-verify` owed by due date |

## Helper Subagents (Hub-and-Spoke)

Phase subagents do not spawn subagents directly. When a phase agent needs codebase exploration, root-cause debugging, schema authoring, or doc drafting:
1. Write the helper brief (`docs/agents-v0/<phase-dir>/<slug>.helper-brief.md`) with `helper:`, `outputs:`, `return:`, and `ask:`.
2. Run `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh <artifact>` to record the `ask:` digest in `helperBriefHashes` (exits 2 if the identical `ask:` was already run).
3. Return to the main session, which runs the helper once, re-launches the phase agent, and deletes the brief upon completion.

## Phase Attempt & Bounce Budgets

- **Build test-failure budget:** Each verify run in Build appends a card to `docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/build-report.md`. Before each attempt, run `sh .agents-v0/scripts/check-attempt-budget.sh docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/build-report.md` (default max 8 failed attempts). Two consecutive failures on the same test require a `failure-brief.md` (`check-failure-brief.sh`) to `debug-investigator`; a third consecutive failure stops Build.
- **Verify → Build bounce budget:** When Verify finds a `Critical` issue, run `sh .agents-v0/scripts/sync-feature-state.sh --verify-passed false --reopen build <artifact>`. If `reopenCount` exceeds 3, stop and escalate to the user.

## Phase Gates Summary

Every phase follows **Reconnaissance → Plan → Execute → Verify → Report** and is guided by its phase skill (`SKILL.md`):

- **Onboard (`/v0-onboard`, `onboard-discovery`):** Brownfield only. Documents the repo as-is (baseline, inventories, module notes, architecture, network, context map) and stops for approval before roadmap, plan, intake, or maintain. A greenfield repo skips this.
- **Roadmap (`/v0-roadmap`, `program-roadmap`):** Sequences discovery items into Now / Next / Later without inventing themes.
- **Architecture (`/v0-architecture`, `program-architecture`):** Writes C4, data flows, ER models, `network.md`, pattern ADR (`Pack: <id>`), `context-map.md`, `nfr-slo.md`, `threat-model.md`, `ops-readiness.md`, `arc-record.md`, and passes `design-reviewer` (`architecture-review.md` with zero `Open` findings). Approval runs `.agents-v0/scripts/activate-stack-pack.sh`.
- **Plan (`/v0-plan`, `program-planning`):** Writes `docs/agents-v0/milestones/plan.md` and `<milestone>.md` with `Surface` and `Size` on each story and acyclic dependencies.
- **Intake (`/v0-intake`, `spec-intake`):** Writes `docs/agents-v0/requirements/<feature>.md` with user story, Gherkin `AC-1`…`AC-8` (including negative/edge scenarios), NFRs, and `Material: yes|no`.
- **Design (`/v0-design`, `contract-first-design`, `ux-design`):** Writes `design.md`, optional `openapi.yaml` / `asyncapi.yaml` / `events/`, ADR, and UX spec/mockups. Stories with contracts, UI, public routes, or `Material: yes` require `design-reviewer` (`review.md` with zero open Criticals) and stop for Design approval. `Contract: None` stories continue to Build.
- **Build (`/v0-build`, `implement-*`):** Verifies a green baseline, writes `docs/agents-v0/build/<feature>/plan.md` mapping every `AC-*` to a test, merges any approved `openapi.yaml` draft into the catalog, implements units via red-to-green TDD, and resolves the bound pack's native verify command with `.agents-v0/scripts/run-backend-verify.sh`. The script only prints. The caller executes the printed command.
- **Verify (`/v0-verify`, `quality-gate`, `vapt-review`, `pr-review`):** `test-engineer` runs the native stack verify command and checks AC test coverage (`quality-gate.md`); then `security-reviewer` (`vapt-checklist.md`) and `code-reviewer` (`code-review.md`) inspect `git diff <baseCommit>...HEAD`. Zero `Critical` findings sets `verifyPassed: true`.
- **Local Release (`/v0-local-release`, `local-release`) & Remote Release (`/v0-release`, `release-pr`):** `/v0-local-release` verifies `verifyPassed: true`, except a maintenance note with `tier: emergency` when `maintain` is approved and the note records a rollback plan and `Follow-up verify due` (full `/v0-verify` stays owed by that date). It re-runs the native verify command on a clean tree, and merges locally (`git merge --no-ff`) after explicit user approval. `/v0-release` prepares and opens a GitLab MR (`glab mr create`) for teams using remote merge requests.

## Rule Precedence

If project files contradict a rule, **the repository wins**. Record approved per-repo exceptions in `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` and ADRs.
